        "id": "condition-2",
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "code": {
          "text": "Pityriasis alba of the face with mild dermatitis and post-inflammatory hypopigmentation"
        },
        "clinicalStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-clinical",
              "code": "active"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Cough"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dry cough for approximately 10 days, starting after an illness with sore throat and blocked nose that has mostly resolved. Worse in the evenings and when talking a lot at work under air conditioning. Patient wondered whether iced coffee and air conditioning are triggers."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated symptoms and pertinent negatives with cough"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No shortness of breath, wheeze, chest tightness, pleuritic chest pain, fevers, chills, or haemoptysis. Appetite okay; energy a bit decreased. Still attending university and work."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Facial skin patches"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Hypopigmented patches on the cheeks for approximately 3–4 months, more noticeable after tanning over summer. Mild intermittent itch, especially after hot showers, with some dryness and flaking. No pain, bleeding, or vesicles. Patient worried about vitiligo and has been scrubbing the face with exfoliant; skin now stings."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Facial skin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Ill-defined hypopigmented macules and patches on both cheeks and lateral jaw, 1–3 cm, with very fine scale on close inspection. Borders not sharply demarcated; background mildly tanned. No complete depigmentation or erythema."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
